Instagram <a href="https://edits.instagram.com/blog/edits-desktop-video-editor/">today expanded</a> its Edits video editing app <a href="https://edits.instagram.com/desktop/">to the Mac</a>. Edits for Mac is intended for larger projects that benefit from a big screen and the control of a mouse and keyboard.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/instagram-edits-mac.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1075936" /><br/>
The app includes Instagram's licensed and royalty-free audio libraries, sound and video effects, and unlimited automatic captions.<br/>
<br/>
Edits for Mac has a full multi-track timeline, keyframes for dynamic transitions, and precise audio waveforms for accurate cuts. There is an option to import LUTs or font files, along with support for Model Context Protocol so AI agents can use the app. The Edits team says splitting, cutting, and trimming are easier.<br/>
<br/>
Videos created with the app can be published directly to Instagram or downloaded to share on other platforms. Multiple horizontal and vertical aspect ratios are included, and Edits offers 4K watermark-free export.<br/>
<br/>
